## CONTEXT BAND AND HANDOVER
At about 70% context start no new step. At about 75% stop at a safe boundary (files whole, every `next start` and Playwright process you started stopped by pid, 9900-9909 free, the lock released) and write `/Volumes/Datasec_DEV/!CODING/Datasec/HPSM-POC/1_Project_Definition/Briefs/2026-11-12_B1541_HANDOVER.md` (done / in hand / next / processes left / decisions a successor keeps: base sha, branch head if pushed, the red set, probe paths), last line `HANDOVER B1541: next step <n> | done steps <list>`, and end STATUS with the same line.

## HARD STOP (slot)
At the HARD STOP clock of the Stamp: start nothing new, push nothing unproven; a committed but unpushed head is `CODED-UNPROVEN b1541/hpsmpoc-three-words <sha40>` in STATUS with the steps that ran; write the HANDOVER and end on its line.

## STATUS and the last line
Sections: STATUS-NOW at the top; BLUF; slots as read; PRIOR WORK; BASE (Step 2 rcs and counts); BUILT (per FROZEN id and per Step-4 item); the byte proof; the red-first list; CI results at BASE and head (each predicate, counts); RENDERED lines; NOT RUN (the `api` jobs, with the reading); FOR TUESDAY (the two "HP-backed tools" comments left in `phase-flow.ts:27` and `PhaseFlow.tsx:101`; the evidence files; any imprecision with its line); resources created and removed; the outside-the-fences disclosure. **LAST line, exactly one of:** `READY B1541: <head sha40>` (equal to `git ls-remote` of the branch), `HANDOVER B1541: next step <n> | done steps <list>`, `STOPPED: <reason>` or `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY <one question>`. While running the last line is `PROGRESS B1541: <step>`.

